[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. It is not one issue.
The reports were merged because their subjects matched ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
not because they share a cause. Read by cause, they hold three problems, and the queued parser fix
closes only one of them.

<SplitTable ticket={4471} filed={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser will not close #4471. The <code>hint</code> and <code>one-day</code> reports stay open until their own fixes ship.
</Callout>

## The three problems

- **`parser`** ([#1](https://github.com/vitorpavani/support-kb-4471/issues/1)): the shared parser reads
  dates month first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. Day and month swap: 7 April shows as 4 July.
- **`hint`** ([#2](https://github.com/vitorpavani/support-kb-4471/issues/2)): the booking-v3 form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month first as told, and the form reads the date
  day first. These are form reports from booking-v3 tenants only, and they need a form fix, not a parser fix.
- **`one-day`** ([#3](https://github.com/vitorpavani/support-kb-4471/issues/3)): the date moves by one day
  and is not swapped ("Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). The desk had already
  noted these in `desk-notes.json`. That looks like a time zone conversion, so it needs a fix of its own.

## How the reports were counted

- **One id, one report.** The export repeats some rows because its pages overlap, so each report is counted once.
- **By tenant, not by intake tag.** The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The cause
  depends on the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`). The table shows how often the tag was wrong.
- **By what the report says.** The one-day moves are the only reports with no swapped day and month.
  The desk's notes flag them, and reading every report body confirms it.

The counts come from `src/lib/kb/split.ts`, which runs at render time. When the desk merges more
reports into #4471, the table updates.

## For the desk

- Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. Re-run this page first.
- Matching on subject merged three bugs into one ticket. Decision 0001 stays as it is, because
  accepted decisions are never edited, but it needs a new record that dedupes by cause.

